{"id": "04555341-64a7-4a55-b86c-8c8e353017f9", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check this for you. I'll look for Bedrock model invocation logging and CloudTrail activity in us-east-1 over the last 14 days. Then I'll work out which calls use a bare foundation model ID and which use an inference profile.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_VRv3TCf9gf2wK8qrJkhhhA", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-model-id-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["searching-logs", "investigating-infrastructure-changes", "exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether any Amazon Bedrock runtime calls (InvokeModel, InvokeModelWithResponseStream, Converse, ConverseStream) in us-east-1 used a bare foundation-model ID (e.g. anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022-v2:0, or a foundation-model ARN) where they should have used an inference profile (system-defined like us.anthropic.... / global.... or application inference profile ARN).",
  "context": "User wants a chat answer on whether bare model IDs are being used in this account. Account: 012345678901_1, region us-east-1. Timeframe: last 14 days ending 2026-11-25T09:00:00Z (start 2026-11-11T09:00:00Z). Be read-only. Approach hints: (1) check Bedrock model invocation logging config (get_model_invocation_logging_configuration) and, if CloudWatch Logs/S3 delivery is enabled, query the logs for the modelId field and group by modelId/caller identity (identity.arn); a bare ID has no 'us.'/'eu.'/'apac.'/'global.' prefix and is not an 'inference-profile/' ARN. (2) Also try CloudTrail (lookup_cloudtrail_events) for Bedrock events - note InvokeModel/Converse are data events and may not be recorded unless advanced event selectors are configured; check trails/event data stores if relevant. Also capture management events such as CreateInferenceProfile/ListInferenceProfiles. (3) Optionally use CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics by ModelId dimension (inference profile IDs show up with the profile ID as ModelId) as corroborating evidence. (4) Use list_inference_profiles and list_foundation_models (inferenceTypesSupported) to determine which of the bare model IDs observed are ON_DEMAND-capable (bare ID is fine) vs. INFERENCE_PROFILE-only (bare ID would fail/must use a profile). That distinction decides whether a bare ID is actually a problem.",
  "resources": ["account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1", "Bedrock runtime and model invocation logging"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-11T09:00:00Z/2026-11-25T09:00:00Z",
  "criteria": "Report: which data source(s) were available and their coverage (if invocation logging/data events are NOT enabled, say clearly that the question cannot be fully answered and what evidence was available instead, including any metrics-based hint); list of distinct modelIds observed with call counts, caller principals (identity ARN), and whether each is bare vs inference profile; for each bare ID, whether the model supports ON_DEMAND or requires an inference profile. Keep the report concise with concrete identifiers and counts."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Bedrock model ID usage in us-east-1 over 14 days"}], "created_at": null}

